> Engraving Elbereth with a fire/lightning wand takes a single
> charge and a single turn like it does with an athame, right?

Takes a single turn and charge, yes.  It's also a permanent (burned-
in) engraving--the athame only does a semi-permanent one.  You can
stand on the burned in one and melee all day long without disturbing
it.  The semi-perm kind will get disturbed fairly soon if you're
meleeing while on it.

> Does it also take a single turn with a hard gem?
No.  1 turn per letter, which makes it nearly useless as an emergency
source of E.  They're also semi-permanent, not truly permanent.


Wands of digging are semi-perm, 1-turn.
Fingers are very temporary, not 100% reliable, but 1-turn.
I believe magic markers are semi-perm, 1 charge, 1 turn, but I'm not
100% on that--I've rarely used them. I know they're at least semi-perm
and they're 1-turn.



